# What RUNS the suite, and nothing else.
#
# Split from `requirements-dev.in` because a single dev lock could not be
# installed beside the runtime one: pip-audit pulls `requests`, which pulls
# `charset-normalizer`, and resolving the two trees together landed 3.5.1 over
# the 3.4.9 that `requirements.txt` pins. `parse_utils` then REFUSED to parse —
# correctly, and loudly — because a parser version the lock does not name is one
# the suite never ran against (AGENTS.md §7). Every test that touches a document
# went red in CI on a tooling dependency.
#
# Install order would have hidden it. Two locks make it impossible instead:
# nothing here shares a dependency with the runtime tree, and a test pins that.
#
#   uv pip compile requirements-test.in --generate-hashes --universal \
#       --python-version 3.12 -o requirements-test.txt
pytest
coverage
